* Covariant / Contravariant / Invariant
  Consider X is a subtype of Y.
  What is the relation between R(X) and R(Y)?

  If it is a subtype then the Relationship R() is called covariant (meaning it preserves the subtyping)

  If it is a supertype, then the Relationship R() is called contravariant (meaning it reverses the subtyping)

  If it is neither, then the Relationship R() is called invariant (meaning it removes the subtyping)
  
  In Java, Arrays are covariant whereas Generics are Invariant.


